From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:43:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] init: extra_free_kbytes.sh: read only each zone's min watermark

The script collects every line of /proc/zoneinfo that contains "min" as
the zones' min watermarks. Newer kernels also print a per-CPU
"high_min:" line in each zone's pagesets, so min[] gets more entries
than managed[] has and min[i] no longer belongs to zone i: on a guest
with DMA32 and Normal zones the Normal zone's term is computed from one
of DMA32's high_min values. high_min follows the low watermark, which
the script itself raises, so every run of it raises the result again.

Read only the zones' own "min" lines, as managed[] does for "managed".

Measured on the Raspberry Pi 5 AAOS guest (3 GiB: DMA32, Normal and an
empty Movable zone, 2026-10-17): 7 lines matched instead of 3;
watermark_scale_factor was 161 after the runs of a boot, and the same
arithmetic on successive runs gives 131, 155, 161, 163. With this
change it is 120, and running the script again leaves it at 120.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 init/extra_free_kbytes.sh | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh b/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh
index a0141be..0edaab2 100755
--- a/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh
+++ b/init/extra_free_kbytes.sh
@@ -98,7 +98,9 @@ extra_free_pg=$((extra_free_kbytes/page_size_kb))
 
 managed=($(grep managed /proc/zoneinfo | awk '{print $2}'))
 length=${#managed[@]}
-min=($(grep "min" /proc/zoneinfo | awk '{print $2}'))
+# Only each zone's own "min" line: a plain grep "min" also matches the per-CPU
+# "high_min:" lines of newer kernels, and min[i] then stops lining up with managed[i].
+min=($(grep -E "^[[:space:]]+min[[:space:]]" /proc/zoneinfo | awk '{print $2}'))
 
 # calculate vm_total_pages.
 # WARNING: if the final low watermark differs from the original, the source of
